Rationale: The claim contains multiple material parts: (1) the dam was completed on July 30, 2012, (2) it was inaugurated by Felipe Calderón, (3) it is one of the biggest waterways in Nayarit, and (4) it is alongside the Mololoa River. The evidence confirms that Felipe Calderón was the Mexican president from 2006-2012, but no evidence directly supports the completion date of the dam, its name, or its location in Nayarit. Additionally, no evidence confirms the dam was inaugurated by Calderón or that it is one of the biggest waterways in Nayarit alongside the Mololoa River. Further investigation is needed to verify these specific details.
